1
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:22,740
Last week at a dinner party, the hostess asked me to sit next to Mrs. Rumbold.

2
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:29,340
Mrs. Rumbold was a large, unsmiling lady in a tight black dress.

3
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:34,730
She d id not even look up when I took my seat beside her.

4
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:42,090
Her eyes were fixed on her plate and in a short time, she was busy eating.

5
00:00:42,090 --> 00:00:44,950
I tried to make conversation.

6
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:49,372
'A new play is coming to "The Globe" soon,' I said.

7
00:00:49,372 --> 00:00:53,120
'Will you be seeing it?'

8
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:55,950
'No,' she answered.

9
00:00:55,950 --> 00:01:02,339
'Will you be spending your holidays abroad this year?'

10
00:01:02,339 --> 00:01:03,230
I asked.

11
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:05,810
'No,' she answered.

12
00:01:05,810 --> 00:01:09,125
'Will you be staying in England?'

13
00:01:09,125 --> 00:01:09,920
I asked.

14
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:12,940
'No,' she answered.

15
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:18,500
In despair, I asked her whether she was enjoying her dinner.

16
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:31,074
'Young man,' she answered, 'if you ate more and talked less, we would both enjoy our dinner!'
